Lately I've been playing pacifists. For me, doing Sokobon is usually
pretty dangerous, as I often don't have a magic whistle for pets, and
if a monster is trapped behind a boulder, it's a royal pain to clear
him out. As such, I generally only do the first half of the first
level (for the scrolls of earth / wand / food), and *sometimes* I go
higher. But it's often just not worth the risk or trouble for me to do
more.

Similarly, I'll go down to Minetown, but I generally find a luckstone
other ways. Only when my character is beefy (post-castle) will I
generally go much lower than Minetown, unless I'm desperate to find a
poly trap for my pet.

